.TH "GLESHA-CONFIGURE" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.nh
.ad l
.SH NAME
glesha\-configure \- change the settings of a backup set
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBglesha configure\fR SET [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Change the saved settings of SET. Only the given options change; new values apply to later runs. Existing snapshots are not rewritten.
.PP
Use \-\-root NAME=PATH to bind an unbound root, such as one from an imported or discovered set, to a directory on this computer. A bound root cannot be rebound.
.PP
The destinations of an incremental set and a catalog that was already published can only be changed with 'glesha move'. Finish pending work before configuring.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-root NAME=PATH
Bind root NAME to directory PATH; repeatable. May be repeated.
.TP
.B \-\-baseline ID
Use snapshot ID as the next incremental's baseline.
.SS Remote options
.TP
.B \-\-to REMOTE...
Upload future snapshots to REMOTE.
.TP
.B \-\-from REMOTE...
Limit bucket access to REMOTE.
.TP
.B \-\-catalog\-to REMOTE|local
Where to keep the catalog.
.PP
REMOTE... takes a comma\-separated list and may be repeated. If \-\-from or \-\-to is given, no other remote is accessed.
.SS Archive options
.TP
.B \-\-storage\-class CLASS
AWS storage class of full snapshots.
.TP
.B \-\-compression FORMAT
Compression: xz, gzip, or bzip2.
.TP
.B \-\-compression\-level N
Compression level, 1 to 9.
.TP
.B \-\-prefix PREFIX
Name prefix: glesha or encb.
.TP
.B \-\-incremental\-storage\-class CLASS
AWS storage class of incremental snapshots.
.TP
.B \-\-chunked
Upload in chunks; \-\-chunked=false turns it off.
.TP
.B \-\-spool\-max SIZE
Local space for chunks (default: 128MiB, min: 2MiB). Requires \-\-chunked.
.SS Passphrase options
.TP
.B \-\-catalog\-passphrase\-file FILE
Read the catalog passphrase from FILE ('\-': stdin). Without this option, GLESHA_CATALOG_PASSPHRASE or a hidden prompt is used.
.PP
The global options described in glesha(1) are also accepted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha configure docs \-\-compression gzip
glesha configure docs \-\-root Documents=~/Documents
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glesha (1),
.BR glesha\-create (1),
.BR glesha\-move (1)
